@* One line in a list that is ticked rather than opened: a box, what it is called, and whatever follows.
   Row's sibling rather than a mode of it - the two look identical and are not the same thing. A Row is
   a <div> or a <button>; this is a <label>, so the whole line hands its press to the box inside it, and
   a <button> may not contain one at all. Four pages wrote it out by hand, and the only differences
   between them were which of the trailing spans they added.

   The press stops here. A tick row can sit inside something else that is pressable - see NoteSummary,
   whose whole card opens the editor - and ticking a line there means ticking that line, not opening the
   note to write in. Nothing is lost where there is nothing above to reach: the other three sit in plain
   cards. *@
<label class="check-row @AdditionalClass" @onclick="() => { }" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
    <input type="checkbox" checked="@IsTicked" disabled="@IsDisabled" aria-label="@AriaLabel"
           @onchange="args => OnTicked.InvokeAsync((bool)args.Value!)" />
    <span class="check-row-text">@Title</span>
    @Trailing
</label>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter] public bool IsTicked { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool IsDisabled { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// What the box alone says, for a reader who never sees the words beside it. Left off where the
    /// title already reads as the whole question - a contact's name in a list of who to add to a group.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string? AriaLabel { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whatever follows the title - a category mark, a meta span, several of each. Row's own Trailing, and for the same reason: how many and which vary by row.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Trailing { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> OnTicked { get; set; }

    /// <summary>"completed" where a ticked row is struck through, and whatever else the caller marks it with.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? AdditionalClass { get; set; }
}
